# Renault Megane I five-door hatchback, 1996-2002.
#
# The first-generation Megane. UK on sale in April 1996, roughly half a year
# after France and hatchback-first; replaced in 2002 by the Megane II. The
# Phase II facelift of 1999 is the shape modelled, because every usable
# reference photograph is of a Phase II car; the object therefore carries the
# generation's UK intro date with the later nose, as the Corolla E120 does.
# https://www.renault.co.uk/ (Megane model page, cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.164 x 1.699 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.580 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes, which give a 4.129-4.164 m length range across Phase I and
# Phase II hatchbacks; the Phase II figure is used. Wheelbase-to-length ratio
# 62.0 per cent. Mirrors extend beyond the 1.699 m hull.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-side elevation but not a true one (its
# apparent wheelbase ratio is 67.7 per cent, so the camera is slightly ahead of
# the side axis); it was used qualitatively for the roof line, waistline, door
# cuts and arches, and the model was compared at that angle. Image 2 supplied
# the Phase II twin grille and swept lamps. Image 3 supplied the tail: a
# distinctly sloped rear glass above a more upright tail panel, which the
# builder correctly preferred to the brief's wording.
#
# Colours are the only British names evidenced: a period newspaper
# (Clitheroe Advertiser & Times, 15 October 1998) lists used Meganes in Iceberg
# Silver, Naples Red, Ascot Green, Goodwood Green, Adriatic Blue, Midnight
# Blue, Capsicum Red, Monaco Blue and Sunflower Yellow, evidence grade (c). No
# Renault UK brochure with a full colour chart was found, so the complete
# palette is grade (d) and no French names have been substituted. Four are
# modelled: Iceberg Silver, Naples Red, Monaco Blue and Ascot Green. Weights
# silver 3, red 3, blue 2, green 2, total 10, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h, the 1.6-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 80/300, on the
# line 180 + 1.5 x 80: a comfortable, quiet family hatchback for its class.
# Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: April 1996 intro, retires staggered 2012-2015 on a
# sixteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-megane-i.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-megane-i.dae (76 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-megane-i/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the lower sill and arch transitions are more angular
# than the photographs, the lamp lenses are shallow, the bumper corners square
# and the tail lamps too short vertically. The top view and eight-view turn
# confirm a continuous body-coloured roof. At 128 px the rounded nose, the tall
# cabin and the sloped hatch glass read as the first Megane.

obj=citycar
name=RenaultMeganeI(IcebergSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1996
intro_month=4
retire_year=2015
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=300

Image[E]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_N.0.0,0,33
Image[NE]=./images/renault-megane-i-icebergsilver_NE.0.0,0,24
